   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Hello\r\nPhil</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">I’m\r\ntrying to estimate a bifactor model with 2 specific factors and it works fine.\r\nWhen a delete a subset of items, it gives the following error. But when I keep\r\nthe subset and put ‘NA’ placeholder instead, it works again. The data is from\r\nlarge scale assessment with multiple matrix sampling and rotated booklet\r\ndesign. Could it be that when I delete the subset, the data becomes sparse and\r\ndisconnected?</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Best</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Maya</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Error\r\nin `vec_slice()`:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">!\r\nCan&#39;t subset elements with `i`.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,sans-serif\">✖</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">\r\nLogical subscript `i` must be size 1 or 6014, not 6002.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin:0in 0in 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Run\r\n`rlang::last_trace()` to see where the error occurred.</span></p></div>\r\n"
    ]
